piness  scale I mean it's a great powerup don't  get me wrong being able to climb up  walls and execute a quick damaging dive  attack is actually quite useful in the  game but if your neighbor Mike decided  to strip down and squeeze his lumpy body  into a tight-fitting cat suit I'm sure  you won't be singing his praises would  you would you don't answer that in Super  Mario Sunshine the game pits you as  Mario against shadow Mario who actually  turns out to be Bowser jr. in disguise  after he drops the charade he also drops  from truth bombs on Mario and Peach  [Applause]  she seems surprised how do you not know  this kind of thing okay let's assume at  least that he's referring to her as a  stepmom since she has spent more than  her fair share of time being held  captive by Bowser  but if jr. is deluded enough to believe  that she is biologically his own mother  that raises way more questions than I'm  comfortable answering in one video look  I don't want to speculate on how that's  even possible any more than you do all I  can say is Bowser jr. certainly has some  daddy issues to work out oh wait he  already knows that Mario and Sonic have  a complicated relationship once  arch-rivals in the early 90s console  wars both spent much of the mid-2000s in  spinoff territory setting the respective  franchises on a collision course that  would see the meet in-game for the very  first time at the Olympics heavy is the  head that wears the crown  yes Mario and Sonic at the Olympic Games  despite being a breakthrough in mascot  ensembles is Peaks spin-off and possibly  rock bottom of both characters crossover  potential two franchises locked in an  eternal battle of BMX races equina  showmanship and track and field  really songs gotta lose a footrace to  peach she's not even touching the ground  Nintendo and Sega have been pretty  consistent in releasing these games  every two years to coincide with the  real world Olympics so it doesn't look  like they're gonna stop anytime soon but  for as weird as the series is you can at  least argue it's all been worth the  effort if only to see why Luigi  performed his graceful rhythmic  gymnastics routine while it may seem  like cheating to reference any game made  for the Philips CDI I mean those zelda  games are still getting crap today for  being made I feel like I have to add  this one to the list nine town T fours  hotel mario is perhaps the most poorly  written and crudely animated mario game  ever made everything about it seems  third-rate and it looks as if it was  cobbled together in ms paint using  rejected assets from the TV show  much like the equally awful Zelda game  for the same platform Hotel Mario is an  FMV adventure filled with plenty of  agonizing cutscenes  when you pitch with these pennies they  pinch back and the gameplay itself finds  Mario traveling to the Koopa family's  collection of boutique hotels which I  can only assume Bowser built with his  own hands since they all seem to fall  apart rather easily also real quick  shouts whoever named these levels the  Chilton blitz snarl tton seizures palace  okay points for these puns  anyway you complete each one of these  levels exactly how you expect in a Mario  game by closing doors I guess it must be  drafting in the building's because in  each hotel you take elevators from floor  to floor shutting every door along the  way that's all the game is yes even as  Bowser himself is breathing down your  neck flames and all you mustn't forget  to close the door behind you but how  about we just forget how it plays and  remember Hotel Mario for all the  wonderful jokes to be made at the  cutscenes expense you know what they say  all toast is toast toast in a stunning  new revelation regarding Super Mario  World it's been revealed by Yoshi's  creator himself that Yoshi is punched in  the head by Mario every time you make  him stick his tongue out  now this sheds new light on their  relationship and makes us all wonder why  the adorable green dinosaur even puts up  with the abuse I mean we know he's  capable of holding his own on the  racetrack so you have to wonder why he  doesn't just up and smack Mario in  return is this how you're gonna treat  the creature that tenderly cared for you  as an infant if that Simpsons Halloween  episode taught us anything it's that  cartoons should stay in cartoons and  transform them into the real world  simply make things look a little odd so  while the Internet has been making a lot  of noise about Mario going off to a  Newark like facsimile city in Super  Mario Odyssey and meeting real humans  Mario's off-kilter proportions versus  real-life people have already been  firmly established in MBA Street vol 3  the game pits Mario Luigi and Peach all  in their round cartoony glory against  players who look like regular humans  Super Mario Odyssey might have brought  more awareness to the characters odd  proportions but it's not the first game  to highlight the fact that despite being  in New Yorker Mario hasn't fit into the  real world in a  long time in speaking of real-world  depictions let's not forget Mario's  unfortunate forays into live-action  productions I'm sure it made sense at  the time to produce a huge summer  blockbuster for one of the most popular  video game characters on the planet but  did they really have to do it like this  aside from the terrible movie and the  questionably accurate TV show tokes  ahead is a hat  Mario also found himself among one of  the most popular television categories  of the late 80s figure skating  on Thursday December 7 1989 those who  are lucky enough to view it witnessed  the strangest and perhaps most hideous  display of videogame marketing ever seen  as the story goes a computer virus opens  up the seventh gate to hell allowing the  baddies from the Mushroom Kingdom ice  skates and all to come pouring into our  world Mario Luigi and Peach follow  shortly after because why the hell not  what follows is roughly 